SampleProject/

# S6 generation sandbox (2026-07-15) — a live, working TIA project used to incrementally build up
# a real generated project via small prompted steps. Same reasoning as SampleProject/: never commit
# the live project folder itself, only whatever gets extracted from it. Anchored to repo root
# (2026-07-16) so the extracted corpus ir/test-project001/ + simatic-ml/test-project001/ CAN be
# committed: Green-tier by construction (docs/13-data-boundary.md, 2026-07-15 GenProject1 entry —
# codenamed test-project001 from 2026-07-17), kept as the durable S6 output and the standing
# validation corpus for reviewer skills (docs/15). The live TIA project folder itself keeps its
# original on-disk name (GenProject1/) for Openness continuity — see CLAUDE.md's codename note.
/GenProject1/

# Never commit Siemens DLLs — reference Siemens.Engineering.dll by install path
Siemens.Engineering*.dll

# Sanitization mapping files (real name -> invented name) — never commit; the point of a
# sanitized artifact is that nothing links it back to the real source, including this
sanitization/

# Real site reference documents (Amber-tier, docs/13-data-boundary.md) — never commit. The
